## Prioritized Remediation Plan

| Priority | Smell | Fix | Effort |
|----------|-------|-----|--------|
| 1 | Assertion-Free (`addAndDoNothing`) | Add assertion | Trivial |
| 2 | Sleepy Test (`addSleepy`) | Delete `Thread.sleep` | Trivial |
| 3 | Exception Handling (`addNullSkuManualCatch`) | Replace with `assertThrows` | Quick |
| 4 | Mystery Guest (`addLoadsFromFile`) | Inline data, remove file I/O | Quick |
| 5 | General Fixture (all tests) | Remove unused `rng` field | Trivial |
| 6 | Conditional Test Logic (`addConditionalLogic`) | Flatten to explicit calls or `@ParameterizedTest` | Moderate |
| 7 | Eager Test (`doEverythingAtOnce`) | Split into focused tests | Moderate |
| 8 | Sensitive Equality (`toStringFormat`) | Assert on semantics, not format | Quick |
| 9 | Magic Number (`quantityAfterAdds`) | Named constants, computed expected | Quick |
| 10 | Ignored Test (`disabledTest`) | Fix or delete | Decision |

Items 1–5 are quick wins that eliminate the highest-risk smells (false passes, flakiness, wasted time). Items 6–10 improve clarity and maintainability.
